### Delivery Service API Tests
### Run with REST Client extension in VS Code or similar tools

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ============= HEALTH CHECKS =============

### Health Check - Overall
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Health Check - Database Only
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/db

### ============= DELIVERY PERSON =============

### Get All Delivery Persons
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryPerson

### Get Active Delivery Persons
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryPerson/active

### Get Delivery Person by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryPerson/1

### Create Delivery Person
POST {{baseUrl}}/deliveryPerson
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "phone": "555-0123",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "isActive": true
}

### Update Delivery Person
PUT {{baseUrl}}/deliveryPerson/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "John Doe Updated",
  "phone": "555-0123",
  "email": "john.doe.updated@example.com",
  "isActive": true
}

### Delete Delivery Person
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/deliveryPerson/1

### ============= DELIVERY ORDERS =============

### Create Order from Monolith
POST {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "orderId": 1001,
  "customerId": 2001,
  "category": "Electronics",
  "idempotencyToken": "order-create-{{$timestamp}}",
  "snapshot": {
    "totalAmount": 299.99,
    "items": ["Laptop", "Mouse"],
    "shippingAddress": "123 Main St, City, Country",
    "customerName": "Jane Customer"
  }
}

### Create Another Order (Food Category)
POST {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "orderId": 1002,
  "customerId": 2002,
  "category": "Food",
  "idempotencyToken": "order-create-food-{{$timestamp}}",
  "snapshot": {
    "totalAmount": 45.50,
    "items": ["Pizza", "Soda"],
    "shippingAddress": "456 Oak Ave, City, Country",
    "customerName": "Bob Smith"
  }
}

### Get All Available Orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder

### Get Available Orders by Category
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder?category=Electronics

### Get Specific Order
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder/1001/2001

### Assign Delivery Person to Order
POST {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder/1001/2001/assign
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "deliveryPersonId": 1,
  "idempotencyToken": "assign-{{$timestamp}}"
}

### Update Order Status
PUT {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder/1001/2001/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "InTransit"
}

### Update Order Status to Delivered
PUT {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder/1001/2001/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "Delivered"
}

### Get Orders by Delivery Person
GET {{baseUrl}}/deliveryOrder/deliveryPerson/1

### ============= TEST SCENARIOS =============

### Scenario 1: Complete Order Flow
### 1. Create delivery person
### 2. Create order
### 3. Get available orders
### 4. Assign delivery person
### 5. Update status to InTransit
### 6. Update status to Delivered

### Scenario 2: Test Idempotency
### Run the same create order request twice with same idempotencyToken
### Should return same result without creating duplicate

### Scenario 3: Category Filtering
### 1. Create orders in different categories
### 2. Filter by specific category
### 3. Verify only matching orders are returned